From 45d7a041e82ce77c3c8e2444eceb31b7c4e742c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 09:19:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: prefer 640x480 explicitly on a Mach64-style
 mode-negotiation miss

Root-caused during the 2026-09 benchmark campaign (docs/BENCHMARK-PLAN.md,
mach64-215ct-2026-09-03.md): a real-hardware ATI Mach64 launch landed on
512x384 instead of the requested 320x240, because that card has no
native 320x240 mode and SDL3's own SDL_GetClosestFullscreenDisplayMode
tie-breaks same-aspect-ratio candidates (320x240/512x384/640x480 are
all exactly 4:3) by always keeping the smallest. Visible on camera as
green dashed banding above the title logo -- leftover VRAM/text-mode
content in a mode this port had never actually validated before.

The only standing mitigation was an ad hoc "SET SDL_HINT_DOS_FORCE_MODE_ID=
0x0111" before each manual benchmark launch, never baked into the
shipped binary -- fine for a controlled benchmark session, not for a
normal player just running DOSSAGE.EXE. A hardcoded FORCE_MODE_ID can't
be baked in unconditionally either: Cirrus and ViRGE both have an exact
320x240 match already and would be actively broken by forcing them onto
640x480 too.

Fix by enumerating available modes ourselves before creating the
window: if the exact request isn't there, prefer 640x480 explicitly
when it's enumerated (the same real-hardware-validated target the ad
hoc FORCE_MODE_ID workaround used), falling back to a generic
same-aspect search only if 640x480 itself isn't available. Cards with
an exact match are untouched -- this block is a no-op for them.

Two real-hardware corrections landed same day (2026-09-10) before this
version, both worth keeping in the record since DOSBox-X cannot
exercise this code path at all (its emulated card has an exact 320x240
match) -- every version had to be found wrong by a real card, not by
emulation:

1. First version picked the LARGEST same-aspect candidate overall,
   reasoning that alone was enough to beat the smallest-first tie-break.
   On this Mach64's UniVBE, which enumerates same-aspect modes all the
   way up through 1280x1024, that overshot to 1024x768 -- the game's
   own 320x240-native content then rendered as a small block in the
   corner of an otherwise-black canvas (confirmed via the rig's room
   camera and DOSVESA-MODESET's own log line).

2. Second version picked the SMALLEST same-aspect candidate that isn't
   smaller than requested -- well-reasoned in the abstract, but for a
   320x240 request on this card, 512x384 IS that smallest candidate,
   and 512x384 is the ORIGINAL corrupted mode this fix exists to avoid.
   A generic closest-without-going-under heuristic has no way to know
   one specific candidate is known-bad; only the real-hardware campaign
   established that. This version encodes that measurement directly
   (explicit 640x480 preference) instead of re-deriving a general rule
   that real hardware kept falsifying.

This is a dossage-local workaround, not a shared-layer fix -- doskutsu
hits the identical SDL3 tie-break on the identical card and carries the
same ad hoc-only mitigation (its own docs/internal/BOOT.md). The
general case (SDL_GetClosestFullscreenDisplayMode's tie-break itself)
would be worth fixing once in the hub's shared SDL3-DOS layer rather
than per-port, but that is a separate, cross-port change; this patch
only unblocks dossage's own real-hardware behavior.
---
 gameSource/game.cpp | 104 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 104 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gameSource/game.cpp b/gameSource/game.cpp
index f506c70..675d108 100644
--- a/gameSource/game.cpp
+++ b/gameSource/game.cpp
@@ -621,6 +621,110 @@ void createScreen() {
     flags = flags | SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN;
     displayW = screenWidth;
     displayH = screenHeight;
+
+    // DOS-PORT: work around SDL_GetClosestFullscreenDisplayMode's own
+    // aspect-ratio tie-break (see SDL_HINT_DOS_FORCE_MODE_ID's doc comment
+    // in SDL_hints.h) always keeping the SMALLEST same-aspect candidate
+    // when the exact requested mode isn't enumerated. Real-hardware
+    // finding (2026-09 benchmark campaign, docs/BENCHMARK-PLAN.md): a card
+    // with no native mode matching screenWidth/screenHeight -- e.g. ATI
+    // Mach64, which has no 320x240 -- lands on a smaller same-aspect
+    // fallback (512x384) instead of the intended larger one (640x480),
+    // visible as leftover-VRAM green corruption above the title logo in
+    // that never-before-cleared mode. Cards with an exact match (Cirrus,
+    // ViRGE) hit no tie at all and are untouched by this block.
+    //
+    // Fix: enumerate the actually-available modes ourselves before
+    // creating the window. If the exact request isn't among them,
+    // prefer 640x480 specifically (VESA-standard mode 0x0111) when it's
+    // enumerated -- the exact fallback this port's whole 2026-09
+    // benchmark campaign validated clean on real Mach64 hardware via an
+    // ad hoc SDL_HINT_DOS_FORCE_MODE_ID=0x0111, now baked in instead.
+    // Falls back to a generic search only if 640x480 itself isn't
+    // available -- a safety net for a card this campaign never tested,
+    // not the primary path.
+    //
+    // Real-hardware correction #1 (2026-09-10): an earlier version of
+    // this fix picked the LARGEST same-aspect candidate overall,
+    // reasoning that was enough to beat the smallest-first tie-break.
+    // On a real Mach64 whose UniVBE enumerates all the way up through
+    // 1280x1024, that overshot to 1024x768, and the game's own
+    // 320x240-native content rendered as a small block in the corner
+    // of an otherwise-black canvas.
+    //
+    // Real-hardware correction #2 (2026-09-10, same day): "smallest
+    // same-aspect candidate that isn't smaller than requested" (the
+    // fix that replaced #1) is well-reasoned in the abstract but wrong
+    // on this specific card: for a 320x240 request, 512x384 IS the
+    // smallest same-aspect candidate that isn't smaller -- and 512x384
+    // is the ORIGINAL corrupted mode this whole fix exists to avoid
+    // (docs/BENCHMARK-PLAN.md's "leftover VRAM/text-mode content not
+    // cleared in this never-before-validated mode" finding). A generic
+    // closest-without-going-under heuristic has no way to know that one
+    // specific candidate is known-bad; only real-hardware measurement
+    // established that, so this version encodes that measurement
+    // directly instead of re-deriving a general rule DOSBox-X can't
+    // exercise (its emulated card has an exact 320x240 match, so this
+    // whole block never fires there) and real hardware then falsifies.
+    {
+        int numModes = 0;
+        SDL_DisplayMode **modes = SDL_GetFullscreenDisplayModes(
+            SDL_GetPrimaryDisplay(), &numModes );
+
+        if( modes != NULL ) {
+            bool exactMatch = false;
+            for( int i=0; i<numModes && !exactMatch; i++ ) {
+                if( modes[i]->w == displayW && modes[i]->h == displayH ) {
+                    exactMatch = true;
+                    }
+                }
+
+            if( !exactMatch ) {
+                bool found640 = false;
+                for( int i=0; i<numModes && !found640; i++ ) {
+                    if( modes[i]->w == 640 && modes[i]->h == 480 ) {
+                        found640 = true;
+                        }
+                    }
+
+                int bestW = 0;
+                int bestH = 0;
+
+                if( found640 ) {
+                    bestW = 640;
+                    bestH = 480;
+                    }
+                else {
+                    double targetAspect = (double)displayW / (double)displayH;
+
+                    for( int i=0; i<numModes; i++ ) {
+                        int w = modes[i]->w;
+                        int h = modes[i]->h;
+                        double aspect = (double)w / (double)h;
+
+                        if( fabs( aspect - targetAspect ) < 0.001 &&
+                            w >= displayW && h >= displayH &&
+                            ( bestW == 0 || w * h < bestW * bestH ) ) {
+                            bestW = w;
+                            bestH = h;
+                            }
+                        }
+                    }
+
+                if( bestW > 0 &&
+                    ( bestW != displayW || bestH != displayH ) ) {
+                    printf( "DOS-PORT: no exact %dx%d mode -- using "
+                            "%dx%d instead of the smallest-first "
+                            "tie-break\n",
+                            displayW, displayH, bestW, bestH );
+                    displayW = bestW;
+                    displayH = bestH;
+                    }
+                }
+
+            SDL_free( modes );
+            }
+    }
 #endif
 
     window = SDL_CreateWindow( "Passage", displayW, displayH, flags );
-- 
2.47.3

